WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:10.940
<b>This 
is
 the
 story</b>

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:10.940
<b>of 
one 
man's
 struggles</b>

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:10.940
<b>and 
his 
growth
—</b>

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:10.940
<b>and
 of
 parenting</b>

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.560
<b>Gen'ichiro</b>

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.860
<i>It's me.</i>

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.630
<i>Are you prepared to join 
the military police?</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.080
<i>We're the only ones who can 
make use of your powers.</i>

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.260
<i>Get over here.</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:50.230
From now on, I work alone.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.680
Oh, God...

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.950
Did they jump?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.700
No, apparently it was a murder.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.290
Shoved out a window.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.130
Come in.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.370
My condolences.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.850
He was a good man.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.490
Thank you for coming, Fukuzawa-san.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.230
By the way, what are these documents?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.740
I'm organizing.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.440
Why?

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:06.280
I suspect that the murderer was intent on 
either stealing or destroying these documents.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.760
In order to confirm that,

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.670
I'm arranging all the documents 
according to any potential patterns.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:18.300
This entire room is a catalog for 
determining the attacker's motivations.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.380
I'm told that he was pushed 
out of this window.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:28.070
The president took me in as a 
secretary. I'm indebted to him.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.870
Solving the nature of the crime would 
be the best farewell gift I can offer.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.260
But, fortunately, the assassin 
has already been captured.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.190
After murdering the president, he was 
apprehended by guards on the first floor,

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.480
and is now being held next door.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.260
What?

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:52.570
The ten fingerprints recovered from the back of 
the president's clothes apparently matched his.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.570
He's still next door?

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.260
He seems to have given up.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.010
He's very quiet.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.920
I'd like to see the assassin.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.210
Be my guest.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.600
But please don't touch the documents.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.820
<i>He's quite an accomplished assassin.</i>

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.400
<i>Reddish hair and dual pistols.</i>

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.340
<i>Which means he must be the child 
assassin so famous in the underground.</i>

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.000
<i>But, if this boy truly is Oda Sakunosuke,</i>

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.140
<i>how could he be captured 
by mere security guards?</i>

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.730
As you can see, that man is 
maintaining his silence.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.030
The municipal police should 
be taking him soon.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.050
As for you—

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.860
Hey, there!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.360
<i>Episode 38</i>

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.360
<b><i>The Lone

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.360
<b><i>m 0 0 l 120 0 120 250 0 230
</i></b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.360
It's damn windy today, huh?

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.570
So, anyway...

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.110
Is there any chance we can 
relocate this company?

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.190
The hills are a pain and the 
directions are so complicated.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.480
Excuse me?

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.850
Also, I'm getting hungry.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:14.780
D'you have any food?

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.170
Excuse me?

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:19.310
Here we go again, looking 
down on me like some kid.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.580
Fine, never mind the food.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.470
Just give me the permit.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.940
Wait, have you lost it 
in all these documents?

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.030
Dammit!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.210
You're the secretary! You'd better find it!

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.390
I don't have the slightest interest 
in the fingerprints in this room.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.690
What is your problem?

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.160
Regardless of the circumstances, 
this is the president's office.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.610
Unless you're authorized, 
you may not be here.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.910
I'm authorized, though.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.740
I'm here for an interview today.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.990
The president did say he would be 
interviewing an administration trainee...

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:56.950
Anyway, I just came here for the working permit 
that I'm supposed to get at the interview.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:00.100
Once I have that, I can get some 
funding from the government.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.790
Mind if I move this useless paper?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.630
You may not!

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.810
The very arrangements of these documents

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:09.620
is a catalog for determining 
the attacker's motivations.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.930
Come on, that's such a blatant lie.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:13.970
Forget it.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.490
I'll find it myself.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.040
I'll be done in an instant.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:17.980
Boy.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:22.030
There's a mountain of documents here. 
How do you plan to find yours?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.350
The old man can speak!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:32.140
Unlike all your loose papers, mine's got a 
heavy stamp and it's printed on thick paper.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.460
Hey!

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:32.900
No!

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.370
Found it.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.360
How could you...

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.010
Now I have to check every sheet 
and arrange it all over.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.980
And I still have to report on the 
missing documents within 48 hours.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.400
Why bother?

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.420
They're all here.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:05.070
No documents have been stolen,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:08.560
and the assassin didn't kill the president.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:12.620
Like, you're the murderer anyway, 
aren't you, secretary?

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:18.910
You arranging documents to keep people away 
so that you can come up with an alibi.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.530
I mean, it's suspicious 
if there were fingerprints

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.330
on the president's clothes but 
nowhere else in the room.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.500
The obviously guilty secretary

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.640
and the obviously innocent 
assassin are right here...

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.220
And you're just standing there.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.880
Come on, mister, you're slacking on the job.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.400
Fukuzawa-san...

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.730
Please kick that kid out of here.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.590
I can't have him making even 
more of a mess in here!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:52.940
The assassin's fingerprints were found 
on the back of the victim's clothes.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.790
From when he shoved him.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.190
There's no way even the best assassin

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:00.240
could get close to the president 
without being noticed.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.460
The door is right in view of the desk.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:08.640
And, if the president resisted before 
he was forced out the window,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.800
the fingerprints would have indicated 
him being thrown out, not pushed out.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.900
He may have happened to 
be looking out the window.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.960
On such a windy day?

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.900
With the window open? By himself?

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.350
<i>He's right.</i>

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:28.450
<i>Which means it must have 
been someone close to him.</i>

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:32.190
It was someone close to him,
 yet the assassin's fingerprints turned up.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.770
So those prints were faked.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:36.980
I heard it's easy to fake fingerprints.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.350
You just need to make molds of the 
fingers using putty or something.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:43.280
Weren't you a police officer or 
something before, mister secretary?

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:46.110
You mentioned the 48 hour 
investigation law earlier.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.290
This is ridiculous!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.450
How would I have taken 
the assassin's prints?!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.510
Fukuzawa-san!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.680
Just get this brat out of here!

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.090
You were able to get the assassin's 
prints because you hired him.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.090
Shut up!

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.810
Since <i>you</i> hired him, you could 
easily entrap a top-tier assassin.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.470
Even get security guards to catch him.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:10.300
I don't think the assassin over there 
even knew he was being entrapped.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.680
I'm sure he'd talk if he 
found out he's been fooled.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.790
Why don't you try asking him?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.240
I have no intention of fighting you.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.940
Don't add more crimes to your guilt.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.110
You can get off with a lesser 
plea if you stop now.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:54.690
What?!

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:01.240
No!

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.670
There is no forgiveness in this world.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.650
Only revenge.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:14.400
You...

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:19.850
Call an ambulance!

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.510
And contact the municipal police!

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.680
I don't think we need to call the ambulance.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.390
The secretary's dead anyway.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:34.600
Miss, could I get another red bean soup?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.280
Why don't you eat the rice cake?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.950
It's not sweet.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.030
When did you realize the 
secretary was the murderer?

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:45.430
From the beginning.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.420
He was wearing a coat, right?

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.620
Who wears a coat when 
they're sorting documents?

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.200
Your sleeves would get in the way.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.270
He was concealing tools for faking 
the assassin's fingerprints.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.190
Boy...

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.670
My name is Edogawa Rampo.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:04.170
Remember that.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.860
What about school?

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:09.110
I was at a police academy, 
living in the dorms.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.900
I had an argument
 with the dorm supervisor,

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.180
so I exposed all of their 
past affairs and I got kicked out.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.400
Since then, I've been bouncing 
around from place to place.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.720
I was a live-in worker at a garrison,

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:26.140
until I got thrown out for blabbing 
about the head chief's corruption.

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:28.650
Your parents?

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:30.670
Dead.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.460
In an accident.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.250
That's why I came out to Yokohama.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.340
Are you full now?

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.970
Yeah, thanks.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:41.790
Good.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.910
Well done today.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.250
That's it?

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:53.060
You're talking to a fourteen-year-old boy 
who's lost his parents, his job and his future.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:54.540
That's all you've got?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.110
<b>Fukuzawa 
Yukichi</b>

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.140
What's that?

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:01.660
My contact information.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:03.790
Security police.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.390
I'm basically a bodyguard.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.820
Contact me if you're ever in trouble.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.320
I'll help you free of charge, 
the first time or so.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:25.480
Boy.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:31.720
Yes?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.970
<i>Help me, mister bodyguard.</i>

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.390
I don't have work or a place to stay.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.960
I'm going to die.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:46.020
I'm headed to work.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.080
Come with me.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:50.410
A client is looking for manpower.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.610
I'll broker a deal for you.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.080
Does that work?

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.580
Really?!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.340
A theater?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:08.470
<b><b>Sekai Gekijou</b></b>

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:08.470
<b><b>Sekai Gekijou</b></b>

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:06.760
The manager has been 
lamenting a staff shortage.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:13.050
If I can finish my job here, 
I'm sure she'd be open to hiring you.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
<b>The 
Day
 Is a
 Dream</b>

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
<b>The 
Night
 Is Real</b>

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.380
What job?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.600
We have some time until opening.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.430
Check the scene for me.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.660
Do you have some idea who the 
threats might be coming from?

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:27.820
The police will do the investigating.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:32.000
Your job is to arrest the 
attacker when it happens.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.060
Could you at least tell 
me what the threat is?

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:36.950
Here.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.450
We received this several days ago.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:46.250
"The angels shall bring true 
death upon the performers. V."

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.620
V?

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.330
The performers, huh?

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.490
So is it the actors who 
are going to be killed?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.140
I can't wait to see what happens.

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:58.400
Who is this child?

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:00.330
He's looking for work.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.370
I heard you needed more people.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:08.870
I'm hoping you can interview him 
once this situation is resolved.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.660
Please send me a resume, then.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.580
I'll evaluate him along 
with the other candidates.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.060
There are other people who signed up?

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.570
There's no chance I'm getting hired, then.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.610
I told you I'll evaluate you.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.320
Nope.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.290
This hag's already decided 
she's not hiring me.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.430
Hag?!

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:28.480
You could have just been honest with me.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.810
Why don't grown-ups ever say 
what they're really thinking?

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.370
Same thing with how you're 
dealing with this guy.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.290
The reason you aren't introducing 
him to the municipal police

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.570
is because you want him to 
keep an eye on the police.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.950
And have the police keep an eye on him.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.330
In other words, you don't trust anyone—

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:45.890
That's enough.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:50.100
I don't care what your intentions are.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.690
I'm simply going to do my 
best to prevent the crime.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.190
I'd like to speak with the staff. 
Is that all right?

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:00.730
Do as you wish.

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.130
Grown-ups are so quick to anger.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:13.250
I'm not surprised you don't 
last long on any job.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>The Day Is a Dream
The Night Is Real {small text on right}</b>

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>Murakami 
Tokio-sama</b>

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:17.180
Why do you speak to me
 right before the show?

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:21.140
Do you know what an actor is 
going through prior to a show?

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.800
We dive into another world.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:27.010
As though we are different people.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:35.490
I've trained for nearly six months for this.

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:38.810
If they mess with me, 
they'll be the dead ones.

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.590
I'll respect your work.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:44.430
But you are the ones who 
may end up murdered.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:47.090
Do you ever end up on your 
own during the performance?

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.160
Yeah.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.800
We're defenseless when we're up there.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.140
I'm on my own for minutes.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.390
Where?

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.420
On the stage.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:00.010
I'm the lead actor, believe it or not.

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:00.790
Huh.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.030
You're the lead actor?

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.360
Murakami... Tokio?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.480
Never heard of you.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.330
Who is that brat?

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.990
Hey, what's this play about?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.110
You've received the script, haven't you?

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.460
That script's boring.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.500
I gave up after the first page.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.450
Boy...

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.890
I see.

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:24.800
If you think it's boring, it must be boring.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.730
That's for the audience 
to decide, after all.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.030
Have you met Murakami?

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:46.600
This play's practically a one-man show.

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:51.270
He's been meeting a lot with the 
stagewright, Kurahashi-san.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:55.280
No one actually thinks there's 
going to be a murder.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.950
But if someone's going to get hit, 
it'd probably be Murakami-kun.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.060
He's got a lot of women 
chasing after him, too.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:03.220
I only have a minor role.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:04.590
I'm not even worth threatening.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:10.610
Maybe I'll become a taxi driver or 
something once this performance is over.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:14.750
You know what that is?

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:15.850
Hm?

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.250
It's an affair.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.820
It's a tiny association.

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:20.680
Maybe they slept with a newcomer.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.830
Or they broke up and quit the group.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:27.720
I'm sure there's a person 
or two they want to kill.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.310
They have potato chips!

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:38.650
And the chocolates I missed out on!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.160
